{"name":"Valentino","hex":"#b64476","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Valentino","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Italian."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A strikingly handsome man, particularly one similar in appearance to Rudolph Valentino.","Synonym of gigolo, a handsome man funded by an older woman."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Valentino"}],"entries":[{"title":"Valentino (surname)","blocks":[{"text":"Valentino is an Italian surname. Notable people with the name include:"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valentino_(surname)"},{"title":"Valentino (given name)","blocks":[{"text":"Valentino is an Italian male given name, the masculine equivalent of the female given name Valentina. It may be abbreviated as \"Vale\" or \"Tino\". The equivalent English male given name is Valentine. A surname, Valentino, also exists."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valentino_(given_name)"},{"title":"Valentino (fashion designer)","blocks":[{"text":"Valentino Clemente Ludovico Garavani, known mononymously as Valentino, was an Italian fashion designer who founded Valentino S.p.A., a luxury fashion house, in 1960 and served as its creative director until 2007. A flamboyant designer noted for his retro pieces and celebrity collaborations, he is regarded as one of the preeminent figures in haute couture."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/80/Valentino_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valentino_(fashion_designer)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Campo_Marzio_-_palazzo_Mignanelli_1150599.JPG/500px-Campo_Marzio_-_palazzo_Mignanelli_1150599.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Campo_Marzio_-_palazzo_Mignanelli_1150599.JPG/1280px-Campo